---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
const lastUpdated = '29 October 2026';
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy and cookies | Andy Whyte Journal"
  description="How the Andy Whyte Journal handles your data, cookies and analytics. Plain English, no nonsense."
  pageType="privacy"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' }]}
>
  <section class="nb-page-head">
    <div class="nb-shell nb-page-head__in">
      <p class="nb-eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy and cookies.</h1>
      <p class="nb-lede">The short version: this site collects the minimum needed to know which Maxims land. No ads, no data sold to anyone, nothing creepy.</p>
      <p class="nb-meta">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="nb-section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="nb-shell">
      <div class="nb-prose">
        <h2>What I collect</h2>
        <p>Two analytics tools run on this site:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, privacy-first and cookieless. It counts pageviews and referrers in aggregate. No cookies, no fingerprinting, no personal data leaves your browser.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Analytics 4</strong>, only if you click Accept on the cookie banner. It is used to understand which Maxims are read, how far through, and which sign-up forms convert. Your IP is anonymised before storage. If you click Decline, or ignore the banner, it runs in cookieless mode: no cookies set, only aggregate signals retained.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Newsletter</h2>
        <p>The journal is published on Substack. When you subscribe, your email address goes to Substack, which sends the entries and handles the data under its own <a href="https://substack.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">privacy policy</a>. Until the Substack publication is connected, sign-ups are collected through Beehiiv under its <a href="https://www.beehiiv.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">privacy policy</a>. You can unsubscribe with one click from any email.</p>

        <h2>Contact form</h2>
        <p>Messages sent through the contact form reach my inbox via <a href="https://resend.com/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Resend</a>. I only use what you send me to reply.</p>

        <h2>Cookies in detail</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Strictly necessary:</strong> none beyond your consent choice and your sound preference for the journal, both stored in your browser's local storage, not as cookies.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics, only after Accept:</strong> Google Analytics sets <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>, used for visit attribution and returning-visitor identification. Retention: 14 months.</li>
          <li><strong>Marketing and ads:</strong> none. This site does not run ads.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Click <strong>Decline</strong> on the cookie banner and no cookies are set.</li>
          <li>Use Google's <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener" target="_blank">opt-out browser add-on</a> for a site-wide opt-out across the web.</li>
          <li>Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> to request access to, correction of, or deletion of any personal data I hold, which is mainly your subscriber email if you have one.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>UK GDPR and PECR</h2>
        <p>This site is operated from the United Kingdom. The lawful basis for processing subscriber emails is your consent: you opted in. The lawful basis for analytics with your consent is also consent; in cookieless mode it is legitimate interest, aggregate site improvement with no personal data stored. You can withdraw consent at any time by clicking Decline or clearing your browser's local storage for andywhyte.com.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Andy Whyte, <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. For any data-protection question, that is the address.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
